From: Ahmed Al-Nassif <mr.ahmed.nassif@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pm: small wakeup/suspend fixes (trimmed for Pixel 9 Pro XL, android14-6.1)

Trimmed from opt.patch. Only the changes that are safe and actually
reachable on Tensor G4 / android14-6.1 GKI with ext4 /data are kept:

 - alarmtimer: hold the wakeup source only until the next alarm
   instead of a fixed 2 s when suspend is aborted.
 - pm_system_wakeup: only kick s2idle on the first abort request.
 - pci: poll PME every 4 s instead of 1 s (fewer wakeups for
   devices that need PME polling).

Dropped: generic lib/string.c routines (not built on arm64), int_sqrt
rewrite (slower than upstream), arm64 prefetch/alignment tweaks,
scheduler tweaks (bypassed by Pixel vendor scheduler), f2fs tunables
(/data is ext4), jbd2 30 s commit age (data-loss risk), 1 s freeze
timeout + locked sysctl (can cause suspend failures), printk/irq log
suppression, _SK_MEM_PACKETS and vfs_cache_pressure changes.
---
 drivers/base/power/wakeup.c | 4 ++--
 drivers/pci/pci.c           | 2 +-
 kernel/time/alarmtimer.c    | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
index 217271324..dca7aaa16 100644
--- a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
+++ b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
@@ -281,7 +281,7 @@ static int alarmtimer_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (ktime_to_ns(min) < 2 * NSEC_PER_SEC) {
-		pm_wakeup_event(dev, 2 * MSEC_PER_SEC);
+		pm_wakeup_event(dev, ktime_to_ms(min) + 1);
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c b/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c
index 770bb04b7ed8b..093fad92e8e51 100644
--- a/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/wakeup.c
@@ -935,8 +935,8 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pm_wakeup_pending);
 
 void pm_system_wakeup(void)
 {
-	atomic_inc(&pm_abort_suspend);
-	s2idle_wake();
+	if (atomic_inc_return_relaxed(&pm_abort_suspend) == 1)
+		s2idle_wake();
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pm_system_wakeup);
 
diff --git a/drivers/pci/pci.c b/drivers/pci/pci.c
index 13dbb405dc31f..814bed9f9ab1f 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci.c
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ struct pci_pme_device {
 	struct pci_dev *dev;
 };
 
-#define PME_TIMEOUT 1000 /* How long between PME checks */
+#define PME_TIMEOUT 4000 /* How long between PME checks */
 
 /*
  * Following exit from Conventional Reset, devices must be ready within 1 sec
-- 
